	<</if>>
</div>

:: D04_Jordan_Text_Polite [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I type, delete, type, delete, type. "Thanks Jordan. That's sweet of you."</p>

<p>I send it, then put the phone down, pick it up, and put it down again.</p>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "So what are you up to tonight? Anything fun?" "">>

<p>"Just chilling at home. Cooking." I don't know why I add the cooking detail. To seem normal, maybe. To seem like a person with a life that involves activities beyond lying in bed questioning her entire existence.</p>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Nice. I'm watching the game with my roommate. He's yelling at the TV. It's a whole thing." "">>

<p>I smile at that, just a small one. "Sounds intense."</p>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "It's always intense. We take our losses personally. Anyway just wanted to say hey. Hope your night is good, Mia." "">>

<p>"Yours too."</p>

<p>The conversation ends there. Natural, easy, no pressure. He didn't push, didn't ask for a photo or a date or anything beyond a few minutes of texting. I read the exchange back. It reads normal. It reads like two people who just met, being casual, being cautious.</p>

<p>This is what people do, I think. They meet. They text. They feel each other out.</p>

<p>My phone sits dark on the cushion. I sit in the quiet.</p>

</div>

<<set $d04JordanTexted to true>>
<<set $jordan.flags.relation to "casual">>

