:: D04_Jordan_Text_Flirty [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I type back without overthinking it, which is either brave or stupid. "You always chase girls on the street? 😏"</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Only the ones I can't stop thinking about." "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The line is corny, objectively corny. Marcus would have cringed. But I don't cringe, because it's directed at me, and corny hits different when you're the target. My stomach does a small, warm flip.</p>

<p>"That's a line."</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Was it good though?" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>"3 out of 10."</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Ouch. I'll workshop it." "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>"You do that."</p>

<p>The texting picks up a rhythm. He asks where I go to school. I tell him the university. He's there too, communications major, senior year. He lives off campus with two roommates in a house he describes as one health code violation away from being condemned. He likes basketball, bad movies, and cooking, which he claims to be good at. I tell him I just made spaghetti for the first time in weeks and he sends back a chef's kiss emoji.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "We should cook together sometime. I make a mean stir-fry." "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The invitation sits on my screen glowing. Together, at his place or mine, in a kitchen, near each other, him tall and me short, and the space between us full of something I can feel through the phone.</p>

<p>"Maybe," I type. The most noncommittal commitment in the English language.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "I'll take a maybe 🙌" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I put the phone down. My face is warm. My stomach is doing the flip thing again. I'm flirting. I, Mia Cole, formerly Marcus Cole, am lying on a couch in panties and an oversized t-shirt flirting with a boy I met on the street hours ago.</p>

<p>The absurdity is total. The feeling is real.</p>

</div>

<<set $d04JordanTexted to true>>
<<set $jordan.flags.relation to "flirty">>
<<run window.statChange("fem", 1)>>

