:: D04_Jordan_Selfie [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Taking a mirror selfie in a dim bedroom, oversized t-shirt slipping off one shoulder" "portrait" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/d04-mirror-selfie.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I open the camera, hold the phone above my face, the angle women do, chin down, eyes up. The girl on the screen looks back at me. Dark hair fanned on the pillow. Hazel-green eyes, wide, a little surprised. Lips slightly parted. The t-shirt's neckline has slipped off one shoulder.</p>

<p>I stare at her for a long time, studying her face the way I've been studying everything about this body. The freckles. The curve of the jaw. The way the pillow light softens everything into something almost pretty.</p>

<p>Almost, no. Not almost.</p>

<p>I take the photo, check it, delete it, take another, and another. Seven photos in two minutes, each with a slightly different angle or expression, each scrutinized and discarded until I find one that looks like a person and not a hostage photo.</p>

<p>I send it, and the three seconds between sending and his response are the longest three seconds of my life.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "holy shit. You're gorgeous." "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The validation hits like a drug, instant and chemical, a flood of warmth that starts in my chest and radiates outward to the tips of my fingers. A stranger thinks I'm gorgeous. A guy who met me for ninety seconds thinks the face he's looking at on his phone right now is gorgeous.</p>

<p>I hate that I like it. I like it anyway. I like it so much that when he sends a shirtless photo back, flexed and grinning in his bathroom mirror, I save it without thinking.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Your turn. Fair's fair 😏" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>My turn. For more. For a body shot, presumably. Me in the t-shirt and panties. The thought makes my pulse hammer in a way that's partly fear and partly something else, something that lives lower than fear, hotter, wetter.</p>

<p>I sit up, pull the shirt down to cover more, then realize that's the wrong direction if I'm actually doing this.</p>

<p>I get up, stand in front of the bedroom mirror, hold the phone at waist height, angled up. The mirror shows me from the thighs up. T-shirt hanging off one shoulder, long enough to cover the panties, legs bare and smooth from today's shave. I look like a girl who just got out of bed, tousled and soft and real.</p>

<p>I take the photo, look at it. It's good. Not posed, not performative, just me standing in my bedroom looking at my phone, the mirror catching it.</p>

<p>I send it before the voice of reason can stop me.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "wow. I cannot believe you talked to me on the street today. I am the luckiest guy." "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The warmth again. The drug again. I lie back on the bed with my phone on my chest and my heart rate elevated and something happening between my thighs that I've been trying not to notice for the last twenty minutes.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Jordan" "😎" "Goodnight gorgeous 😘" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I type "goodnight" and add a 😊 and agonize over the emoji for thirty full seconds before sending it. Is the smiley too eager? Too casual? Too much? Not enough? Would a 😘 back be an escalation or a reciprocation? Does it matter? Why do I care?</p>

<p>I send it anyway and put the phone on the nightstand, screen down. The room is dark. My body hums with something that isn't quite arousal and isn't quite happiness and isn't quite fear. It's all three, braided together, vibrating at a frequency I've never felt before.</p>

</div>

<<set $d04SentSelfie to true>>
<<run window.statChange("cor", 2)>>

